WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:03.000
-Thank you for being here buddy.
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.033
-It is always great to see you.
You look great.

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.901
-Thank you.
-Last time we talked,

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:08.100
you were telling me that you
were into these ice baths.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.033
You remember this?
I have a photo of you.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:13.868
Here's you in your friend's
trash can.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.300
-Oh, yeah, the trash bin.
-With ice.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:19.400
-And it was like, all about
breathing and freezing yourself.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.534
-It was good. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:22.534
It's good for the body,
a good reset.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:24.601
Good for training.
-Yes, gets the blood moving.

00:00:24.601 --> 00:00:27.534
-I actually, I was doing it
the other day

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:28.934
with a buddy of mine,

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.567
and when you're doing it
in a bin like that,

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:33.567
you're putting 120 pounds
of ice in, a bunch of water,

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.934
but it's not that cold.

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:37.634
It's probably like 40 degrees.
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.767
-My buddy has one that's
32 degrees,

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:40.968
which is 0 degrees Celsius,

00:00:40.968 --> 00:00:42.701
for anybody who's watching
over there.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.300
That's, like,
freezing temperature.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.367
So I got into it, and I hadn't
done it in, like, 6 months.

00:00:48.367 --> 00:00:50.734
I'm sitting there, and after,
like, two minutes, suddenly --

00:00:50.734 --> 00:00:52.801
by the way, screaming, like,
I was yelling.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.734
I was like, "Ahh!"

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.300
I was like, "I can't move.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.534
Why's my body locking up?"

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.467
It felt like the blood
was freezing in my body.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.234
Obviously, it wasn't.
-You froze yourself?

00:01:04.234 --> 00:01:06.667
-I'm a bit of a drama queen,
clearly, but...

00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:08.400
-So you're still continuing
to do this?

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:09.934
-Yeah, I love it.
I think it's great.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.300
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.701
-Sounds fun. Sounds amazing.

00:01:12.701 --> 00:01:13.968
Give me a second to get
back into it.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.033
Once you get back into it,
it's --

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.400
-I want to talk about
"Black Adam."

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:19.667
I'm so excited. Everyone's so
excited for this movie.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.734
And you were telling me
something funny backstage.

00:01:21.734 --> 00:01:24.501
'Cause you have a great sense of
humor and you're very fun.

00:01:24.501 --> 00:01:27.200
Every time you've come on,
we've done bits, joked around.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:28.701
-Water gun fight.
-Yeah. We've done everything.

00:01:28.701 --> 00:01:30.267
Can you tell everyone what you
were telling me?

00:01:30.267 --> 00:01:32.167
There was a big action scene.
-Yes.

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.534
-You have to run 40 yards.
-Yes, yes.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:36.234
-With all these parked cars,
and then you have to run back.

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:37.334
-The other way.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:39.100
-You're wearing your
superhero costume?

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.434
-Full, in garb, right?

00:01:40.434 --> 00:01:42.868
Everything's covered.
It's 100 degrees outside.

00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:44.434
It's Atlanta, you know?

00:01:44.434 --> 00:01:45.701
It's humid.
-Those suits get hot, right?

00:01:45.701 --> 00:01:47.434
-Well, yeah, yeah.

00:01:47.434 --> 00:01:50.067
There's no, like -- the skin
is totally covered,

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:52.868
which looks badass.
-Yeah, of course.

00:01:52.868 --> 00:01:55.033
-But when you're doing
wind sprints --

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:57.167
-Look at this.
This is that I'm talking about.

00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:59.934
-Yeah.
-That's what I'm --

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:01.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.667 --> 00:02:04.133
Alright, so you're running
through 100 degrees.

00:02:04.133 --> 00:02:06.200
-We did, you know, we did not
that many takes.

00:02:06.200 --> 00:02:07.501
We did six takes,
and they're like,

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:09.067
"Should we do one more?
I'm like, "Yeah, you know.

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.300
Why not? I'm game. This is --"

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:13.834
You only get to do this
so many times, right?

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:14.968
So I'm like,
"Yeah, let's do it again."

00:02:14.968 --> 00:02:17.767
So I'm running, and I go,
"This time...

00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:18.801
let's make it funny, right?"

00:02:18.801 --> 00:02:20.133
Let me try to make it funny.

00:02:20.133 --> 00:02:22.767
So I'm running off the curb.
There's a parked car.

00:02:22.767 --> 00:02:26.234
I pretend to hit my knee
on the parked car

00:02:26.234 --> 00:02:27.467
as I'm running.

00:02:27.467 --> 00:02:30.200
And I spin around like,
"Ahh," like that hurt.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.901
My arm goes up,
and then dislocates.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:36.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:38.200
-Dude, that's --
-Fully out of socket.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.167
I'm like, "It'll go back in.
Hold on. Hold on.

00:02:41.167 --> 00:02:42.968
I'm gonna move it back in."

00:02:42.968 --> 00:02:44.534
It did not go back in.

00:02:44.534 --> 00:02:46.000
-So now it's not a joke.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.467
-No, so, well now, yeah.
Exactly.

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.901
Now I'm like, "Okay, hold on.
Stop, stop, stop running."

00:02:49.901 --> 00:02:52.567
And keep in mind, the suit
is tight, right?

00:02:52.567 --> 00:02:54.834
It's like a glove fit.
-Yeah.

00:02:54.834 --> 00:02:56.601
-And so they're like,
"What's wrong?"

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:58.234
I'm like, "My arm's
out of its socket."

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.868
So they go down and they're
trying to get it.

00:02:59.868 --> 00:03:00.968
It's not going back in,

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.000
so they have to
cut the suit open.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.601
They open it up,
they take it down.

00:03:04.601 --> 00:03:07.133
I'm sitting there like, "I can't
believe this is so funny."

00:03:07.133 --> 00:03:11.667
And 13 tries later,
with a foot in my armpit

00:03:11.667 --> 00:03:13.734
and a guy pushing from behind,
they just --

00:03:13.734 --> 00:03:14.934
whoom.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.834
It goes back in finally, right?
[ Crowd groans ]

00:03:16.834 --> 00:03:20.133
And I'm like, "Woo, yeah!"
Throw my arms in the air.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.601
I'm like, "We're back in!"

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:24.367
When my arm goes in the air,
it dislocates again.

00:03:24.367 --> 00:03:25.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.868 --> 00:03:29.601
-That's the best story.
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:29.601 --> 00:03:31.901
All because you wanted to
do some funny bit.

00:03:31.901 --> 00:03:33.400
[ Laughter ]
Why not?

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.667
-So they were like,
"Let's try it again."

00:03:34.667 --> 00:03:37.634
I was like, "Fire in the hole!"
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:37.634 --> 00:03:39.300
-They got it on the third time.

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.901
It went back in
and that was that.

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.601
So yeah, it was an action movie
for sure.

00:03:42.601 --> 00:03:44.534
-Yes, it is.

00:03:44.534 --> 00:03:46.234
Well, let's talk
about this movie.

00:03:46.234 --> 00:03:47.501
This is "Black Adam,"

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.601
who, of course, is played
by Dwayne Johnson.

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.834
-Man.
-And we love him. Oh, my God.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:54.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:57.167
-You're a tall guy.
You're a big dude.

00:03:57.167 --> 00:03:59.434
I would say, next to...
-I'm like, uh...

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.934
You know, compared to him.
-Yeah, no. Yeah.

00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:03.200
-He's pretty big, but...
-Yeah.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.167
-I'll tell you this, though.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.901
I might be smaller than him.

00:04:06.901 --> 00:04:10.767
The moment I saw him,
I had one thought in my head.

00:04:10.767 --> 00:04:12.367
"I could take him."
-Wow!

00:04:12.367 --> 00:04:13.534
-Yeah.
-Really?

00:04:13.534 --> 00:04:15.234
-I'm looking at him,
he's looking at me.

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.501
I'm going,
"Oh, I could [bleep] you up."

00:04:17.501 --> 00:04:20.834
-Oh, my God! No, no, no.
That is not true.

00:04:20.834 --> 00:04:22.868
How far away were you
when you said that?

00:04:22.868 --> 00:04:24.133
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:26.267
-He might have been, like,
500 feet away, but...

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.300
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
That's smart. That's smart.

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.133
He's one of the greatest guys
to hang out with.

00:04:31.133 --> 00:04:32.234
-The best.
-Did you end up picking up

00:04:32.234 --> 00:04:33.701
any of his mannerisms?

00:04:33.701 --> 00:04:35.467
Can you do the eyebrow raise?
-Oh, the little -- the thing?

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:36.934
I don't know. Should we try it?
-Yeah.

00:04:36.934 --> 00:04:38.467
[ Clears throat ]

00:04:38.467 --> 00:04:40.067
Ooh, hey!

00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:41.267
That's actually not bad!

00:04:41.267 --> 00:04:42.334
[ Applause ]

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:44.200
That's great!
-I do it like --

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:46.200
-Also Pierce Brosnan.
-Wait, can you do it?

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:48.467
-I think I --
-Can you do the eyebrow thing?

00:04:49.767 --> 00:04:53.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.434
-Can't really do it.

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:56.701
I can't really do it.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:58.501
-I don't know which eyebrow
is worse.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.968
I can't.
I'm blinking on that one.

00:05:00.968 --> 00:05:03.567
Pierce Brosnan,
also in the movie.

00:05:03.567 --> 00:05:05.334
-Pierce Brosnan, yeah, no.
It's an amazing cast.

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:07.901
-Do you get intimidated,
'cause, I mean,

00:05:07.901 --> 00:05:09.667
he is James Bond.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:09.667 --> 00:05:11.767
Hard to not be
intimidated by him.

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:13.167
He's a titan in the industry.

00:05:13.167 --> 00:05:15.701
-He's a cool customer?
-Just cool.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:18.133
That's the thing about
Dwayne and Pierce, though,

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:21.267
is that their reputations
precede them,

00:05:21.267 --> 00:05:23.067
that they're these
magnanimous people.

00:05:23.067 --> 00:05:24.834
And then you meet them,
and they're so disarming.

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:28.567
They're so kind,
and they're just so supportive.

00:05:28.567 --> 00:05:30.033
-Yeah.
-And they're fun to work with.

00:05:30.033 --> 00:05:33.267
I remember one time,
Piece, we were getting ready.

00:05:33.267 --> 00:05:34.567
Everyone's in character.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.868
We're on the Hawk Cruiser,
which is insane, right?

00:05:36.868 --> 00:05:38.767
You're introduced to
all these new characters,

00:05:38.767 --> 00:05:39.901
and we're sitting there,
and they're, "Alright.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.200
Should we shoot the rehearsal?"

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.267
And he just leans over to me
and he goes,

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:46.000
[ Clears throat ]

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.667
[ As Pierce Brosnan ]
"They're all rehearsals."

00:05:47.667 --> 00:05:49.434
-Yeah!
-I was like...

00:05:49.434 --> 00:05:51.267
-That's the secret of acting.

00:05:51.267 --> 00:05:53.968
The secret of acting is,
they're all rehearsals.

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:55.067
-I was like,
"You're so right, dude."

00:05:55.067 --> 00:05:56.367
-Yeah.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.300
How do we set up what's
happening in "Black Adam"?

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.667
-Mm, uh, okay.

00:05:59.667 --> 00:06:04.667
You got this, the original god
chosen by the gods,

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.501
Black Adam,

00:06:06.501 --> 00:06:10.267
who's been asleep for
5,000 years, gets woken up

00:06:10.267 --> 00:06:14.501
and starts to wreak havoc, and
so the Justice Society, who --

00:06:14.501 --> 00:06:16.067
this is the first time
for Black Adam

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:18.667
in the cinematic universe as
well as the Justice Society,

00:06:18.667 --> 00:06:22.100
which predates even the Justice
League, 1940s, I believe.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:26.734
They get -- We get recruited.

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:28.934
So it's Hawkman,
it's Dr. Fate.

00:06:28.934 --> 00:06:31.000
They're on the Justice Society.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:33.567
And then they recruit
Atom Smasher and Cyclone

00:06:33.567 --> 00:06:35.834
to come and take care of
Black Adam,

00:06:35.834 --> 00:06:37.601
see what's going on.
-Yeah.

00:06:37.601 --> 00:06:40.334
And could you ever see maybe
a spin-off for Atom Smasher?

00:06:40.334 --> 00:06:42.234
-I would [bleep] love to.

00:06:42.234 --> 00:06:43.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.767 --> 00:06:46.767
You guys, it's up to you!
-Yeah, it's up to the fans!

00:06:46.767 --> 00:06:47.968
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:50.334
Here's Noah Centineo
in "Black Adam."

00:06:50.334 --> 00:06:51.400
Take a look at this.

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:52.968
♪♪

00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:54.133
-That is insane.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.200
[ Monitor warbling ]

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:56.734
-The nanobots did
most of the work.

00:06:56.734 --> 00:06:59.434
-No, no, no. I'm not gonna
let you downplay it.

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:01.834
I literally just witnessed
a miracle.

00:07:01.834 --> 00:07:03.501
-[ Scoffs ]
-What?

00:07:03.501 --> 00:07:04.901
Did I say something stupid?
-No.

00:07:04.901 --> 00:07:07.901
It's just, you can transform
your molecular structure,

00:07:07.901 --> 00:07:09.434
grow 100 times your own size.

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:12.434
You're an impossibility,
and the world still amazes you.

00:07:12.434 --> 00:07:14.300
I don't know, it's...

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:16.000
It's cool.

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.300
-Thank you.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:21.100
But it's not as cool
as nanobots.

00:07:21.100 --> 00:07:23.634
-Yeah! Noah Centineo!

00:07:23.634 --> 00:07:27.701
"Black Adam" is in theaters
and IMAX October 21st!

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:29.901
We'll be right back with
more "Tonight Show," everybody.

00:07:29.901 --> 00:07:31.133
Stick around! Come on back.

